From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the VM's windows follow the displays once they settle (#428)

What: every display change (the main window changing screen, entering or
leaving full screen, the screen parameters, the guest's word) asks for an
update of the displays' windows, and it runs from one timer once the
displays settle (ui/omacvm-display-settle.h): never inside the notification
that asked, never inside another update, never while the screen is locked,
the displays sleep or another user has the console (then 1 s after unlock or
wake; all three are also read at start, where no notice comes). Displays
that are inactive, asleep or smaller than 100 x 100 points count as absent;
one that comes back gets its window once it has counted for 2 s. Full-screen
tries are counted per display, also when its window is made again: 4 tries,
a pause doubling from 1 s between them, a full screen that held 10 s starts
the count over. A display window that goes while macOS moves it into or out
of full screen is closed once macOS is done (or after 4 s). A display window
whose Space macOS moved to another display is made again on its own.
resizeWindow never runs inside itself, the main window's size check after a
resize runs a moment later, a size macOS keeps refusing is tried 3 times,
and nothing is sized for a display that does not count.
OMACVM_TEST_LOCK_HOOK=1: the distributed notifications org.omacvm.test.lock
and org.omacvm.test.unlock stand for the lock (tests; the test Mac is never
locked).

Why: #428 (@ylorn): the VM in full screen on a MacBook's display and an
external one, the Mac locked, the external display unplugged (or waking
inactive at 1 x 1 for 3 s): macOS moved the main window's full-screen
Space, its setFrame: posted a resize whose check sized the window again
(29 deep), the window changed screen inside that, the screen change ran the
display update at once, the second display's window was made again, each
new one went into full screen in a new Space (the 5-try cap was per window)
and was closed in the middle of it, so AppKit kept it and its Space: 33 to
89 black full-screen Spaces in half a minute, until QEMU quit.

Upstream: not sent (the extra displays' windows are OmacVM's).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-display-settle.sh (the rules, and the
wiring in the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time); src/tests/e2e/display-unplug.sh
(windows and Spaces counted while a display goes, flaps and comes back).

